INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2815,16796623585306,2207,50725,NULL,'en_US','<table>\u000a\u0009<tbody>\u000a\u0009\u0009<tr>\u000a\u0009\u0009\u0009<td align="left">Yes, we are always looking to expand our network of retail partners. If you are interested in stocking our eyewear, please contact our sales team for more information.</td>\u000a\u0009\u0009</tr>\u000a\u0009\u0009<tr>\u000a\u0009\u0009</tr>\u000a\u0009</tbody>\u000a</table>',NULL)
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2816,16796623585306,2208,50735,'availableLanguageIds',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2817,16796623585306,2208,50735,'defaultLanguageId',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2818,16796623585306,2209,50735,NULL,'en_US','','<table>\u000a\u0009<tbody>\u000a\u0009\u0009<tr>\u000a\u0009\u0009\u0009<td align="left">Yes, we have partnered with various optical shops where you can try on our eyewear. Please visit our website to find the nearest location.</td>\u000a\u0009\u0009</tr>\u000a\u0009\u0009<tr>\u000a\u0009\u0009</tr>\u000a\u0009</tbody>\u000a</table>')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2819,16796623585306,2210,50745,'availableLanguageIds',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2820,16796623585306,2210,50745,'defaultLanguageId',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2821,16796623585306,2211,50745,NULL,'en_US','','<p>We offer a wide range of eyewear including prescription glasses, sunglasses, and contact lenses. We also have a collection of designer frames to suit different styles and preferences.</p>')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2901,16796623585306,2301,50907,'availableLanguageIds',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2902,16796623585306,2301,50907,'defaultLanguageId',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2903,16796623585306,2302,50907,NULL,'en_US','<p>Hey there, all you cool cats and trendy peeps! Let''s talk about the hottest trends in eyewear that are sweeping the nation (and your Instagram feed) right now. From oversized frames to bold colors, there''s something for everyone to rock this season.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>First up, oversized frames are reigning supreme in the eyewear game. Think big, bold, and oh-so-chic. Whether you''re channeling your inner ''70s diva with some oversized square frames or going for a more modern look with some round frames that take up half your face, bigger is definitely better when it comes to eyewear right now.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>But if oversized isn''t your thing, fear not! Sleek and slim frames are also making a comeback. Think wire frames or thin, round frames that add a touch of sophistication to any outfit. These frames are perfect for those who want to make a statement without going overboard.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>Now, let''s talk about color. Gone are the days of basic black and tortoiseshell frames. It''s all about bold, bright colors now. From vibrant reds and yellows to soft pastels and even neon hues, there''s a rainbow of options to choose from. So why not have some fun with your eyewear and add a pop of color to your everyday look?</p>\u000a\u000a<p>And let''s not forget about the rise of clear frames. These transparent frames are a modern twist on a classic style and are a great way to add a subtle yet stylish touch to your outfit. Plus, they pretty much go with anything, so you can''t go wrong with a pair of clear frames in your collection.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>It''s not just about the frames, though. Lenses are also getting in on the trend game. From blue light-blocking lenses to mirrored finishes, there are plenty of options to choose from to up your eyewear game. Blue light-blocking lenses are perfect for those long days spent staring at screens, while mirrored finishes add a touch of edge to any look.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>So, how are these trendy eyewear styles being received by the public? Well, it seems like everyone is on board with the oversized frames trend. They''re seen on celebrities, influencers, and fashionistas alike, and it''s clear that they''re here to stay. Slim frames are also getting a lot of love for their sleek and sophisticated look.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>When it comes to color, people are embracing the rainbow of options available. Whether it''s a subtle pastel or a bold neon, there''s a hue for everyone to rock with confidence. And clear frames? Well, let''s just say they''re definitely a hit for their versatility and modern appeal.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>In conclusion, the latest trends in eyewear are all about making a statement and having fun with your look. Whether you''re into oversized frames, bold colors, or sleek designs, there''s a trend out there for you to try. So go ahead, pick out a new pair of specs that scream "you," and strut your stuff with confidence. Because when it comes to eyewear, the bolder, the better!</p>',NULL)
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2904,16796623585306,2303,50918,'availableLanguageIds',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2905,16796623585306,2303,50918,'defaultLanguageId',NULL,'','en_US')
INSERT INTO DDMFIELDATTRIBUTE VALUES(0,0,2906,16796623585306,2304,50918,NULL,'en_US','<p>Annual eye exams are an essential part of maintaining good eye health and overall well-being. Many of us take our eyesight for granted, but the reality is that our eyes are complex organs that require regular care and attention. Just like we visit the dentist for regular check-ups and the doctor for physical exams, scheduling an annual eye exam should also be a priority.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>One of the most important reasons to have an annual eye exam is early detection of eye diseases and conditions. Many eye diseases, such as glaucoma, macular degeneration, and diabetic retinopathy, often have no early symptoms. By the time symptoms do appear, the disease may have already progressed to a point where irreversible damage has occurred. However, through a comprehensive eye exam, an eye care professional can detect early signs of these conditions and provide treatment to prevent further damage and preserve vision.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>Moreover, annual eye exams are not just about checking for eye diseases; they also play a crucial role in monitoring your overall health. The eyes can provide valuable insights into your overall health, as they can reveal underlying health conditions such as diabetes, high blood pressure, and even certain types of cancer. In some cases, an eye care professional may be the first to detect signs of these systemic diseases during a routine eye exam, leading to early diagnosis and treatment.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>Furthermore, regular eye exams can help ensure that your eyeglass or contact lens prescription is up to date. Our vision can change over time, and even small changes in prescription can make a significant difference in how well you can see. By having an annual eye exam, you can ensure that you are seeing as clearly as possible, which is essential for performing daily tasks, driving safely, and maintaining overall quality of life.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>In addition to the functional benefits of annual eye exams, they also provide an opportunity to discuss any concerns or questions you may have regarding your eye health. Your eye care professional can offer advice on how to protect your eyes from digital eye strain, UV exposure, and other environmental factors that can impact your vision. They can also provide guidance on proper eye care habits, such as wearing protective eyewear during sports or using lubricating drops for dry eyes.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>It is important to remember that annual eye exams are not just for those with existing eye conditions or vision problems. Everyone, regardless of age or eye health status, can benefit from regular eye exams. Children should have their first comprehensive eye exam at six months of age, followed by another at three years old, and then before starting school. Adults should have annual eye exams, while adults over the age of 60 should consider biannual exams due to the increased risk of age-related eye diseases.</p>\u000a\u000a<p>In conclusion, annual eye exams are a vital component of maintaining optimal eye health and overall well-being. By scheduling regular eye exams, you are taking proactive steps to protect your vision, detect potential health issues early, and ensure that you are seeing clearly. So, make your eye health a priority and schedule your next eye exam today. Your eyes will thank you for it!</p>',NULL)
